BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventbackfromthedeadcemeterywalk8942-20261009@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261017T133525Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261009
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Back from the Dead Cemetery Walk
DESCRIPTION:On this unique and popular Cemetery Walk\, as a guide leads you through the dark by candlelight\, saints and other characters come to life and reflect upon the “Last Things”: death\, judgement\, heaven\, and hell. Through these encounters you’ll discover what it means to truly be alive\, both now and in the life to come. This faith-filled walk is ideal for youth groups and families with older children (14+). What to expect on the outdoor Cemetery Walk: This walking experience lasts for 1 hour and takes place primarily in the dark. All paths are wheelchair / stroller accessible. No seating is available throughout the experience. In the event of inclement weather\, all tickets will be refunded or rescheduled to another night\, pending availability.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/back-from-the-dead-cemetery-walk/8942/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventlegends26lore26224-20261009@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261017T133525Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261009
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Legends & Lore
DESCRIPTION:Come see the darker side of Frederick. When night falls\, Frederick’s familiar streets have rather different stories to tell. Climb aboard our vintage double-decker for an hour of dark tales from Frederick’s past\, researched from local histories\, old accounts and the legends that have lingered long after the people involved have gone. As we make our way through the city\, we’ll slow down at the very places connected to these stories\, from historic streets and old buildings to some of Frederick’s more famously haunted places. Along the way\, you’ll hear tales of strange happenings\, restless spirits and the darker chapters of local history\, all told against the backdrop of Frederick after dark. And because it’s October\, you’ll also get a rather good view from the top deck as the city’s historic homes and neighborhoods put on their best autumn and Halloween displays. Whether you’re a believer\, a skeptic\, or simply enjoy a good story with a slightly unsettling ending\, Legends and Lore offers a different way to discover Frederick’s history. Just remember\, it’s much easier to laugh at a ghost story when you’re not sitting on the top deck in the dark. TOUR HIGHLIGHTS Hear researched tales of Frederick’s haunted places\, local legends and darker history\, told where the stories happened. Experience Frederick after dark from the top deck\, with historic streets\, autumn displays and a few places you’ll look at rather differently afterwards. TOUR DETAILS Price: $35 per person Duration: 1 hour Recommended Age: 14+ Departure: RAK Brewing Co\, 400 Sagner Ave\, Frederick\, MD\, 21701
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/legends-%26-lore/26224/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventhauntedhistoryatthenationalmuseumofcivilwarmedicine15484-20261010@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261017T133525Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Haunted History at The National Museum of Civil War Medicine
DESCRIPTION:Starting on October 10th\, tour the most haunted building in Frederick – the National Museum of Civil War Medicine. Explore the building’s history amidst the darkened galleries and offices. On the tour\, staff and volunteers will share stories of Civil War embalmers\, the building’s most infamous tenants\, and their first-hand accounts of paranormal activity that have given the building its spooky reputation. In addition to a trip through the museum galleries\, the tour provides exclusive access to the third floor where numerous sightings have occurred. 48 East Patrick Street was built in the 1830s. Before it became the National Museum of Civil War Medicine\, the building was a furniture shop and a site of Civil War embalming\, as well as home to many Frederick residents and their businesses. The past still echoes through the halls of the building. The haunting sights\, sounds\, and sensations from the building have been reported for decades by the people who lived and worked in the building over many years. Join us to hear our staff and volunteers’ stories first-hand. You are invited to bring your own cameras and ghost-finding apps – who knows what you’ll capture! Flash photography and LIVE streaming are prohibited. Tours will be given on October 10\, 17\, 24\, and 25\, from 5:30 p.m.-6:30 p.m. This year we are offering two special Halloween tours on Saturday\, October 31\, from 5:30 p.m.-8:00 p.m. and 8:00 p.m.-10:30 p.m. During these special Halloween night tours\, you’ll have additional time to tour the galleries without a guide.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/haunted-history-at-the-national-museum-of-civil-war-medicine/15484/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgevent72filmfest20954-20261016@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261017T133525Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:72 Film Fest
DESCRIPTION:Year 21! Lights. Camera. Chaos! Or should we say…FUN! The annual 72 Film Fest returns to the Weinberg Center for Year 21\, and the pressure is still the same: teams of filmmakers have just 72 Hours to write\, shoot\, and edit a complete short film from scratch. The theme and criteria (details of what must be included or avoided) are not revealed until the Launch Party. Creativity meets a ticking clock and the results are always impressive\, hilarious\, moving\, and completely unpredictable. All local entries premiere Friday night at the Weinberg Center. Then\, finalists and award winners return for the big Saturday Night Main Event followed by the award ceremony. Keep an eye out for special Saturday Matinee screenings as well. From first-time filmmakers and students to seasoned pros\, come out and cheer on your favorites. Give some love to the incredibly talented folks right here in Frederick\, and beyond! Wondering about this year’s theme?…We’ll say one thing: 21. Learn more about 72 Film Fest by visiting their official website. Friday Night Premieres - All Local Films Premiere over two blocks: 6:30pm\, 8:30pm Saturday Main Event - 12:30pm\, 3:30pm (Special Screenings)\, 7pm (Finalists and Award Ceremony)
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/72-film-fest/20954/
END:VEVENT
