DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:2026 Exhibits at Museum of Frederick County History
DESCRIPTION:Take a deep dive into various topics that have defined Frederick's history\, as we celebrate America's 250th anniversary and our County's role in the Revolution. Featuring brand new exhibits: Cultivating Independence: Frederick in the Revolution Witnessing Revolution All Saints Street: Avenue to the History of Frederick and Its African American Community Growing Gold: A History of Frederick’s Goldfish Industry And returning favorites: Etchison Connections Timeless Toys 24 E Church Street Decorative Arts See our all new and renovated exhibits\, March 7\,2026 through December 12\, 2026. Buy tickets here.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/2026-exhibits-at-museum-of-frederick-county-history/24908/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventalleynights23158-20261017@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261017T133525Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:Alley Nights
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to Alley Nights — your Saturday night destination in Downtown Frederick. With three bars open\, the party moves wherever the night takes you! Start in our newly renovated Main Bar\, catch the DJ spinning in Terrace\, or head upstairs to the rooftop bar for drinks and views of downtown Frederick. Add late-night bites\, great music\, and a lively crowd — and you’ve got everything you need for the perfect Saturday night! Benefactor Events joins us every first and third Saturday of the month to get the party going in Terrace! Meet us at Alley Nights! No cover | 21+ event.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/alley-nights/23158/
