BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventexhibitopeningwherelightsettles3awalterbartmanranageralis26nathanielwilliams26244-20261017@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261017T133525Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:Exhibit Opening - Where Light Settles: Walter Bartman\, Rana Geralis\, & Nathaniel Williams
DESCRIPTION:Three nationally recognized\, highly regarded painters will be at the gallery to discuss their work and process and to answer questions for this special exhibition featuring new paintings. All three painters were recently featured in the September and October issues of American Art Collector Magazine\, through their representation at Lockhouse Gallery. Walter Bartman founded the Yellow Barn Studio in Glen Echo\, Maryland where he is currently the director. He has mentored and taught thousands of accomplished painters. He paints in plein air\, particularly around Frederick County\, near his home studio. His work is kept in national and international collections. Rana Geralis is a plein air landscape painter and also specializes in equine subjects. She is a master of the palette knife\, which allows for thick\, vibrant applications of paint in her work. Rana participates in many plein air competitions and has won numerous awards in the field. She also teaches painting at the Yellow Barn Studio. Nathaniel Williams is a well-known American Realism painter who is represented nationally through galleries\, shows\, and museums. He paints local scenes in Brunswick and Frederick County areas. His work has gained major popularity at the Affordable Art Fair in Chelsea\, New York City. Don't miss this opportunity to hear their process and ask them questions!! Light Food\, Wine\, and Beverages will be served. This is a casual and free event.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/exhibit-opening-where-light-settles%3a-walter-bartman-rana-geralis-%26-nathaniel-williams/26244/
END:VEVENT
