UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventhogwartsatthehaven26068-20261017@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261017T133525Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:Hogwarts at the Haven
DESCRIPTION:For one unforgettable evening\, The Elk’s Haven will be transformed into a world of candlelight\, magic\, mystery\, and feasting. Step through the doors and leave the ordinary world behind as you enter a spectacular wizarding dinner experience inspired by the magic of an enchanted school. Guests will be welcomed into a breathtaking Great Hall filled with floating candles\, long banquet tables\, glowing lanterns\, magical décor\, and hidden surprises throughout the evening. Your night will include: A dramatic candlelit Great Hall House assignments and friendly competition A magical multi-course feast Specialty wines\, cocktails\, and enchanted drinks available for purchase Interactive magical experiences Wand-worthy photo opportunities House points and a final winning-house celebration Free glass of wine\, beer or cocktail Come dressed in your finest robes\, gowns\, cloaks\, or magical attire and prepare for an evening where fantasy comes to life. Whether you arrive as a seasoned wizard\, curious witch\, mischievous student\, or magical creature\, there will be a place waiting for you at the table. Gather your friends. Choose your robes. Your invitation to the Great Hall has arrived.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/hogwarts-at-the-haven/26068/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventhotbrass26coolgrooves26096-20261017@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261017T133525Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:Hot Brass & Cool Grooves
DESCRIPTION:Spires Brass Band kicks off its season welcoming 5 time Grammy nominated bassist and Frederick native Scott Ambush as featured soloist. While Scott’s roots are distinctly Frederick\, for over 30 years he has traveled the world performing with the dynamic jazz fusion group Spyro Gyra. This will be a concert for the ages that you don’t want to miss! Please note that this event “Hot Brass & Cool Grooves” will be at Frederick High School (from which Scott and many Spires members graduated).
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/hot-brass-%26-cool-grooves/26096/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventintroductiontogelliplateprinting26216-20261017@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261017T133525Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:Introduction to Gelli Plate Printing
DESCRIPTION:Learn the creative possibilities of Gelli plate printing in this fun\, beginner-friendly workshop. Whether you're new to printmaking or looking to add fresh techniques to your artistic practice\, you'll learn how to make vibrant\, one-of-a-kind monoprints using a flexible Gelli printing plate. Through demonstrations and hands-on exploration\, you'll experiment with layering colors and shapes\, creating hand-cut stencils\, transferring images\, and registering multiple layers to produce richly textured\, expressive prints. A Gelli plate is a soft\, reusable printing surface that makes monoprinting simple and accessible\, allowing you to create unique prints without the need for a traditional printing press. By the end of the workshop\, you'll have completed a collection of original prints while gaining the skills and confidence to continue exploring this versatile printmaking process at home. What to Bring: All basic materials are provided\, including Gelli plates\, paints\, paper\, and printing supplies. Students are encouraged to bring items that create interesting textures or patterns\, such as stencils\, rubber stamps\, bubble wrap\, corrugated cardboard\, lace\, or other textured fabrics and materials. Experience Level: No previous printmaking experience is necessary. This workshop is suitable for students ages 15 and up.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/introduction-to-gelli-plate-printing/26216/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
