BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventmyersvillefarmersmarket21730-20261017@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261017T133525Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:Myersville Farmers Market
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate local products\, fresh food\, and community at the Myersville Farmers Market! Explore seasonal fruits and vegetables\, fresh mushrooms\, meats eggs and cheeses\, baked goods\, local honey\, local spirits\, bath and body products\, locally made crafts\, and more! The purpose of these markets is to build community spirt and engagement\, as well as and to increase relationships between the artisans\, crafters\, and farmers with their customers.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/myersville-farmers-market/21730/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventoktoberfestatschifferstadt11763-20261017@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261017T133525Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
SUMMARY:Oktoberfest at Schifferstadt
DESCRIPTION:Rain or shine! Free entry. Join us for our most popular event\, an important fundraiser for the operation of our organization and upkeep of Schifferstadt. Come enjoy great food and drink\, lively German music\, historic demonstrators\, tours of the museum\, and hand-made products from many arts & crafts vendors. Our biggest event of the year!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/oktoberfest-at-schifferstadt/11763/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventpumpkinpatchtrains26popuponpenn26154-20261017@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261017T133525Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:Pumpkin Patch Trains & Pop Up on Penn
DESCRIPTION:Pumpkins & Pop Up on Penn brings two fall favorites together in Walkersville! Enjoy a festive Pumpkin Patch Train ride with the Walkersville Southern Railroad\, then explore Pop Up on Penn\, an open-air market featuring local vendors\, makers\, artists\, and food trucks. Come shop local\, grab something delicious\, and make a day of it at the train station!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/pumpkin-patch-trains-%26-pop-up-on-penn/26154/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventjumbospumpkinpatchfallfestival11483-20261018@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261017T133525Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
SUMMARY:Jumbo's Pumpkin Patch Fall Festival
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the season with a full day of festive fun for all ages at Jumbo’s Pumpkin Patch! From classic farm adventures to fall-themed attractions\, our Fall Fun Festival is the perfect weekend outing for families\, friends\, and pumpkin lovers. What’s Included with Admission: Your ticket includes unlimited access to a variety of seasonal attractions: Hayrides through the farm 30+ acre u-pick pumpkin patch (pumpkins sold by the pound) Corn maze (14 acres) Petting zoo Jumping pillow Giant slides Mini mazes for younger guests Playgrounds and yard games General Store with fall shopping and décor​ Optional Add-Ons: (Available for Purchase Onsite - Saturday and Sunday Only) Enhance your day with these fun extras: Pony Rides – $7 Face Painting – $4 Sandy Candy (Edible Sand Art) – $4 Corn Cannon – $5 (3 shots) ​ Food & Drinks: Come hungry! A variety of food\, snacks\, and beverages are available for purchase\, including selections from Liquidity Ale Works of Mt. Airy. Tickets available online or at the gate.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/jumbos-pumpkin-patch-fall-festival/11483/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventmoonfestivalalice25830-20261018@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261017T133525Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
SUMMARY:Moon Festival Alice
DESCRIPTION:MET's FUN COMPANY PRESENTS: Moon Festival Alice - A MET Original A curious child falls down a rabbit hole during a Mid-Autumn Festival celebration and enters a magical world inspired by Asian folklore\, festivals\, and modern Asian American life. Presented in partnership with The Asian American Center of Frederick. RUN TIME: Around an hour with no intermission.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/moon-festival-alice/25830/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgevent2026exhibitsatmuseumoffrederickcountyhistory24908-20261022@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261017T133525Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261022
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261023
SUMMARY:2026 Exhibits at Museum of Frederick County History
DESCRIPTION:Take a deep dive into various topics that have defined Frederick's history\, as we celebrate America's 250th anniversary and our County's role in the Revolution. Featuring brand new exhibits: Cultivating Independence: Frederick in the Revolution Witnessing Revolution All Saints Street: Avenue to the History of Frederick and Its African American Community Growing Gold: A History of Frederick’s Goldfish Industry And returning favorites: Etchison Connections Timeless Toys 24 E Church Street Decorative Arts See our all new and renovated exhibits\, March 7\,2026 through December 12\, 2026. Buy tickets here.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/2026-exhibits-at-museum-of-frederick-county-history/24908/
END:VEVENT
